411	  /**
412	   * This method is used to get an alternate type adapter for the specified type. This is used to
413	   * access a type adapter that is overridden by a {@link TypeAdapterFactory} that you may have
414	   * registered. This feature is typically used when you want to register a type adapter that does a
415	   * little bit of work but then delegates further processing to the Gson default type adapter. Here
416	   * is an example:
417	   *
418	   * <p>Let's say we want to write a type adapter that counts the number of objects being read from
419	   * or written to JSON. We can achieve this by writing a type adapter factory that uses the {@code
420	   * getDelegateAdapter} method:
421	   *
422	   * <pre>{@code
423	   * class StatsTypeAdapterFactory implements TypeAdapterFactory {
424	   *   public int numReads = 0;
425	   *   public int numWrites = 0;
426	   *   public <T> TypeAdapter<T> create(Gson gson, TypeToken<T> type) {
427	   *     TypeAdapter<T> delegate = gson.getDelegateAdapter(this, type);
428	   *     return new TypeAdapter<T>() {
429	   *       public void write(JsonWriter out, T value) throws IOException {
430	   *         ++numWrites;
431	   *         delegate.write(out, value);
432	   *       }
433	   *       public T read(JsonReader in) throws IOException {
434	   *         ++numReads;
435	   *         return delegate.read(in);
436	   *       }
437	   *     };
438	   *   }
439	   * }
440	   * }</pre>
441	   *
442	   * This factory can now be used like this:
443	   *
444	   * <pre>{@code
445	   * StatsTypeAdapterFactory stats = new StatsTypeAdapterFactory();
446	   * Gson gson = new GsonBuilder().registerTypeAdapterFactory(stats).create();
447	   * // Call gson.toJson() and fromJson methods on objects
448	   * System.out.println("Num JSON reads: " + stats.numReads);
449	   * System.out.println("Num JSON writes: " + stats.numWrites);
450	   * }</pre>
451	   *
452	   * Note that this call will skip all factories registered before {@code skipPast}. In case of
453	   * multiple TypeAdapterFactories registered it is up to the caller of this function to ensure that
454	   * the order of registration does not prevent this method from reaching a factory they would
455	   * expect to reply from this call. Note that since you can not override the type adapter factories
456	   * for some types, see {@link GsonBuilder#registerTypeAdapter(Type, Object)}, our stats factory
457	   * will not count the number of instances of those types that will be read or written.
458	   *
459	   * <p>If {@code skipPast} is a factory which has neither been registered on the {@link
460	   * GsonBuilder} nor specified with the {@link JsonAdapter @JsonAdapter} annotation on a class,
461	   * then this method behaves as if {@link #getAdapter(TypeToken)} had been called. This also means
462	   * that for fields with {@code @JsonAdapter} annotation this method behaves normally like {@code
463	   * getAdapter} (except for corner cases where a custom {@link InstanceCreator} is used to create
464	   * an instance of the factory).
465	   *
466	   * @param skipPast The type adapter factory that needs to be skipped while searching for a
467	   *     matching type adapter. In most cases, you should just pass <i>this</i> (the type adapter
468	   *     factory from where {@code getDelegateAdapter} method is being invoked).
469	   * @param type Type for which the delegate adapter is being searched for.
470	   * @since 2.2
471	   */
472	  public <T> TypeAdapter<T> getDelegateAdapter(TypeAdapterFactory skipPast, TypeToken<T> type) {
473	    Objects.requireNonNull(skipPast, "skipPast must not be null");
474	    Objects.requireNonNull(type, "type must not be null");
475	
476	    if (jsonAdapterFactory.isClassJsonAdapterFactory(type, skipPast)) {
477	      skipPast = jsonAdapterFactory;
478	    }
479	
480	    boolean skipPastFound = false;
481	    for (TypeAdapterFactory factory : factories) {
482	      if (!skipPastFound) {
483	        @SuppressWarnings("ReferenceEquality")
484	        boolean isSkipPast = factory == skipPast;
485	        if (isSkipPast) {
486	          skipPastFound = true;
487	        }
488	        continue;
489	      }
490	
491	      TypeAdapter<T> candidate = factory.create(this, type);
492	      if (candidate != null) {
493	        return candidate;
494	      }
495	    }
496	
497	    if (skipPastFound) {
498	      throw new IllegalArgumentException("GSON cannot serialize or deserialize " + type);
499	    } else {
500	      // Probably a factory from @JsonAdapter on a field
501	      return getAdapter(type);
502	    }
503	  }
