505	  /**
506	   * This method serializes the specified object into its equivalent representation as a tree of
507	   * {@link JsonElement}s. This method should be used when the specified object is not a generic
508	   * type. This method uses {@link Class#getClass()} to get the type for the specified object, but
509	   * the {@code getClass()} loses the generic type information because of the Type Erasure feature
510	   * of Java. Note that this method works fine if any of the object fields are of generic type, just
511	   * the object itself should not be of a generic type. If the object is of generic type, use {@link
