1140	   * specified type. It is not suitable to use if the specified class is a generic type since it
1141	   * will not have the generic type information because of the Type Erasure feature of Java.
1142	   * Therefore, this method should not be used if the desired type is a generic type. Note that this
1143	   * method works fine if any of the fields of the specified object are generics, just the object
1144	   * itself should not be a generic type. For the cases when the object is of generic type, invoke
1145	   * {@link #fromJson(JsonElement, TypeToken)}.
