1188	  }
1189	
1190	  /**
1191	   * This method deserializes the JSON read from the specified parse tree into an object of the
1192	   * specified type. This method is useful if the specified object is a generic type. For
1193	   * non-generic objects, use {@link #fromJson(JsonElement, Class)} instead.
1194	   *
1195	   * @param <T> the type of the desired object
1196	   * @param json the root of the parse tree of {@link JsonElement}s from which the object is to be
1197	   *     deserialized
1198	   * @param typeOfT The specific genericized type of src. You should create an anonymous subclass of
1199	   *     {@code TypeToken} with the specific generic type arguments. For example, to get the type
1200	   *     for {@code Collection<Foo>}, you should use:
1201	   *     <pre>
1202	   * new TypeToken&lt;Collection&lt;Foo&gt;&gt;(){}
1203	   * </pre>
1204	   *
1205	   * @return an object of type T from the JSON. Returns {@code null} if {@code json} is {@code null}
1206	   *     or if {@code json} is empty.
